    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 703.3pt; border-collapse: collapse; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" width=\"938\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 106.35pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"142\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>MPATH-Dx&nbsp;v2.0 class</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 198.95pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Risk of tumour progression<br />(probability of progression, No.&nbsp;per population)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 199.0pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Treatment recommendation</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 199.0pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Examples<sup>a</sup></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 106.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"142\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>0</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 198.95pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&ndash;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 199.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Consider repeat biopsy</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 199.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Non-diagnostic/unsatisfactory</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 106.35pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"4\" width=\"142\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Class&nbsp;I</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Low-grade</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 198.95pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"4\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Very low risk for continued proliferation and progression to invasive melanoma</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">(1&nbsp;in&nbsp;10<sup>4</sup> to 1&nbsp;in&nbsp;10<sup>5</sup>)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 199.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"4\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">No further treatment<sup>b</sup></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 199.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Common acquired naevi, no atypia</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 199.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Congenital naevi, no atypia</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 4; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 199.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Atypical and dysplastic naevi, low-grade atypia<sup>c</sup></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 5; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 199.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Common blue naevus</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 6; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 106.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"6\" width=\"142\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Class&nbsp;II</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>High-grade</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 198.95pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"6\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Low risk for progression to invasive melanoma</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">(1&nbsp;in&nbsp;10<sup>2</sup> to 1&nbsp;in&nbsp;10<sup>3</sup>)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 199.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"6\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Re-excision of incompletely excised lesions with margins &lt;&nbsp;10&nbsp;mm<sup>b</sup></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 199.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Atypical and dysplastic naevi, high-grade atypia<sup>c</sup></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 7; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 199.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Spitz naevus, Spitz melanocytoma (atypical Spitz tumour)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 8; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 199.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Cellular blue naevus, atypical cellular and other blue naevi, melanocytomas</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 9; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 199.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">WNT-activated deep penetrating / plexiform melanocytoma (naevus)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 10; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 199.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Lentigo maligna</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 11; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 199.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Melanoma in&nbsp;situ</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 12; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 106.35pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"142\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Class&nbsp;III</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Melanoma pT1a</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 198.95pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Relatively low risk for local and regional metastasis</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">(1&nbsp;in&nbsp;10 to 1&nbsp;in&nbsp;10<sup>2</sup>)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 199.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Follow national guidelines, e.g. excision with 10&nbsp;mm margins<sup>b</sup></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 199.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Melanoma AJCC stage pT1a</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&lt;&nbsp;0.8&nbsp;mm Breslow thickness:</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span lang=\"PT\">Melanoma pT1a&nbsp;lr<sup>d</sup></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span lang=\"PT\">Melanoma pT1a<sup>e</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 13; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 106.35pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"142\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Class&nbsp;IV</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Melanoma &gt;&nbsp;pT1b</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 198.95pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Moderate to increased risk of regional and/or distant metastasis (1&nbsp;in&nbsp;2 to 1&nbsp;in&nbsp;10)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 199.0pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Follow national guidelines, e.g. excision with 10&ndash;20&nbsp;mm margins<sup>b</sup>; consider sentinel lymph node staging and therapies</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 199.0pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Melanoma AJCC stage pT1b or &gt;&nbsp;0.8&nbsp;mm Breslow thickness</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">AJCC,&nbsp;American Joint Committee on Cancer; lr,&nbsp;low risk.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup>a</sup>Examples do not constitute a comprehensive list of diagnostic terms. <sup>b</sup>Margins are considered positive and the lesion adequately sampled. <sup>c</sup>Low-grade atypia connotes naevi (or other lesions) previously graded as mild and moderate (not all), and high-grade atypia naevi (or other lesions) previously graded as moderate (not all) and severe. Degree of atypia is defined by both architectural disorder and cytological atypia. <sup>d</sup>pT1a&nbsp;lr (low risk)&nbsp;&ndash; radial growth phase (Clark level&nbsp;II) only; absence of ulceration, vertical growth phase, dermal mitotic activity, and extensive regression (&gt;&nbsp;50% of tumour). <sup>e</sup>Conventional pT1a risk category (does not qualify as low risk pT1a&nbsp;lr).</p>",
